{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"code","value":"function createOptimisticAction<TVariables>(options): (variables) => Transaction;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/db/blob/main/packages/db/src/optimistic-action.ts#L54","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/db/src/optimistic-action.ts:54"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Creates an optimistic action function that applies local optimistic updates immediately\nbefore executing the actual mutation on the server."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This pattern allows for responsive UI updates while the actual mutation is in progress.\nThe optimistic update is applied via the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onMutate"},{"type":"text","value":" callback, and the server mutation\nis executed via the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"mutationFn"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Important:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" Inside your "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"mutationFn"},{"type":"text","value":", you must ensure that your server writes have synced back\nbefore you return, as the optimistic state is dropped when you return from the mutation function.\nYou generally use collection-specific helpers to do this, such as Query's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"utils.refetch()"},{"type":"text","value":",\ndirect write APIs, or Electric's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"utils.awaitTxId()"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"type-parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"tvariables","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TVariables"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TVariables"},{"type":"text","value":" = "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"unknown"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The type of variables that will be passed to the action function"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"options"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../interfaces/CreateOptimisticActionsOptions.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"CreateOptimisticActionsOptions"}]},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TVariables"},{"type":"text","value":">"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Configuration options for the optimistic action"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"returns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A function that accepts variables of type TVariables and returns a Transaction"}]},{"type":"code","value":"(variables): Transaction;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"parameters-2","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"variables","children":[{"type":"text","value":"variables"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TVariables"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"returns-2","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../interfaces/Transaction.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Transaction"}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"example","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const addTodo = createOptimisticAction<string>({\n  onMutate: (text) => {\n    // Instantly applies local optimistic state\n    todoCollection.insert({\n      id: uuid(),\n      text,\n      completed: false\n    })\n  },\n  mutationFn: async (text, params) => {\n    // Persist the todo to your backend\n    const response = await fetch('/api/todos', {\n      method: 'POST',\n      body: JSON.stringify({ text, completed: false }),\n    })\n    const result = await response.json()\n\n    // IMPORTANT: Ensure server writes have synced back before returning\n    // This ensures the optimistic state can be safely discarded\n    await todoCollection.utils.refetch()\n\n    return result\n  }\n})\n\n// Usage\nconst transaction = addTodo('New Todo Item')","lang":"ts"}],"headings":[{"id":"type-parameters","text":"Type Parameters","level":2},{"id":"tvariables","text":"TVariables","level":3},{"id":"parameters","text":"Parameters","level":2},{"id":"options","text":"options","level":3},{"id":"returns","text":"Returns","level":2},{"id":"parameters-2","text":"Parameters","level":3},{"id":"variables","text":"variables","level":4},{"id":"returns-2","text":"Returns","level":3},{"id":"example","text":"Example","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\nfunction createOptimisticAction<TVariables>(options): (variables) => Transaction;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/db/src/optimistic-action.ts:54](https://github.com/TanStack/db/blob/main/packages/db/src/optimistic-action.ts#L54)\n\nCreates an optimistic action function that applies local optimistic updates immediately\nbefore executing the actual mutation on the server.\n\nThis pattern allows for responsive UI updates while the actual mutation is in progress.\nThe optimistic update is applied via the `onMutate` callback, and the server mutation\nis executed via the `mutationFn`.\n\n**Important:** Inside your `mutationFn`, you must ensure that your server writes have synced back\nbefore you return, as the optimistic state is dropped when you return from the mutation function.\nYou generally use collection-specific helpers to do this, such as Query's `utils.refetch()`,\ndirect write APIs, or Electric's `utils.awaitTxId()`.\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TVariables\n\n`TVariables` = `unknown`\n\nThe type of variables that will be passed to the action function\n\n## Parameters\n\n### options\n\n[`CreateOptimisticActionsOptions`](../interfaces/CreateOptimisticActionsOptions.md)\\<`TVariables`\\>\n\nConfiguration options for the optimistic action\n\n## Returns\n\nA function that accepts variables of type TVariables and returns a Transaction\n\n```ts\n(variables): Transaction;\n```\n\n### Parameters\n\n#### variables\n\n`TVariables`\n\n### Returns\n\n[`Transaction`](../interfaces/Transaction.md)\n\n## Example\n\n```ts\nconst addTodo = createOptimisticAction<string>({\n  onMutate: (text) => {\n    // Instantly applies local optimistic state\n    todoCollection.insert({\n      id: uuid(),\n      text,\n      completed: false\n    })\n  },\n  mutationFn: async (text, params) => {\n    // Persist the todo to your backend\n    const response = await fetch('/api/todos', {\n      method: 'POST',\n      body: JSON.stringify({ text, completed: false }),\n    })\n    const result = await response.json()\n\n    // IMPORTANT: Ensure server writes have synced back before returning\n    // This ensures the optimistic state can be safely discarded\n    await todoCollection.utils.refetch()\n\n    return result\n  }\n})\n\n// Usage\nconst transaction = addTodo('New Todo Item')\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: createOptimisticAction\ntitle: createOptimisticAction\n---\n\n```ts\nfunction createOptimisticAction<TVariables>(options): (variables) => Transaction;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/db/src/optimistic-action.ts:54](https://github.com/TanStack/db/blob/main/packages/db/src/optimistic-action.ts#L54)\n\nCreates an optimistic action function that applies local optimistic updates immediately\nbefore executing the actual mutation on the server.\n\nThis pattern allows for responsive UI updates while the actual mutation is in progress.\nThe optimistic update is applied via the `onMutate` callback, and the server mutation\nis executed via the `mutationFn`.\n\n**Important:** Inside your `mutationFn`, you must ensure that your server writes have synced back\nbefore you return, as the optimistic state is dropped when you return from the mutation function.\nYou generally use collection-specific helpers to do this, such as Query's `utils.refetch()`,\ndirect write APIs, or Electric's `utils.awaitTxId()`.\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TVariables\n\n`TVariables` = `unknown`\n\nThe type of variables that will be passed to the action function\n\n## Parameters\n\n### options\n\n[`CreateOptimisticActionsOptions`](../interfaces/CreateOptimisticActionsOptions.md)\\<`TVariables`\\>\n\nConfiguration options for the optimistic action\n\n## Returns\n\nA function that accepts variables of type TVariables and returns a Transaction\n\n```ts\n(variables): Transaction;\n```\n\n### Parameters\n\n#### variables\n\n`TVariables`\n\n### Returns\n\n[`Transaction`](../interfaces/Transaction.md)\n\n## Example\n\n```ts\nconst addTodo = createOptimisticAction<string>({\n  onMutate: (text) => {\n    // Instantly applies local optimistic state\n    todoCollection.insert({\n      id: uuid(),\n      text,\n      completed: false\n    })\n  },\n  mutationFn: async (text, params) => {\n    // Persist the todo to your backend\n    const response = await fetch('/api/todos', {\n      method: 'POST',\n      body: JSON.stringify({ text, completed: false }),\n    })\n    const result = await response.json()\n\n    // IMPORTANT: Ensure server writes have synced back before returning\n    // This ensures the optimistic state can be safely discarded\n    await todoCollection.utils.refetch()\n\n    return result\n  }\n})\n\n// Usage\nconst transaction = addTodo('New Todo Item')\n```\n"}
